{#
   THE STATE CHIP — the coloured word in a card's head, in one place.

   Parameters:

     label   the word, already translated ("Libre", "Hors service", "Terminée")
     signal  go | wait | caution | stop | muted — see the vocabulary table in
             `_catalogue_card.html.twig`. ⚠️ A SIGNAL, never a class name and
             never a colour: the caller says what it means, this file decides
             how it looks.

   ⚠️ It exists because `reservation-detail.html.twig` needs the same chip as the
   catalogue card but is not a card, and was writing `ml-state-{{ tone }}` by
   hand with the raw class names. Two places interpolating class names is how a
   vocabulary drifts the first time one of them gains a value the other lacks.

   ⚠️ An unknown signal falls back to `muted` rather than emitting a class that
   does not exist. A chip with no colour rule inherits body text and silently
   reads as "closed" — better to be deliberately grey than accidentally so.
#}
{% set _chip = {
    'go':      'free',
    'wait':    'busy',
    'caution': 'caution',
    'stop':    'down',
    'muted':   'closed',
} %}
{% if label|default('') %}
    <span class="ml-state ml-state-{{ _chip[signal|default('muted')]|default('closed') }}">
        <span class="ml-dot"></span>{{ label }}
    </span>
{% endif %}
